# Everything git already ignores at the repository root (.dart_tool/, build/,
# .flutter-plugins*, …) still applies: those patterns live in the root
# .gitignore, a different file from this one, and pub only replaces the
# .gitignore *of this same directory* — which does not exist — not the
# root's. Verified by dry-run: neither directory appears in the archive with
# or without this file.
#
# example/pubspec_overrides.yaml is local-only, the same way pub already
# treats every package's own pubspec_overrides.yaml: it points at sibling
# packages by path (../../dartway_client, …), which do not exist in a
# downloaded archive. Named explicitly rather than relying on pub's own
# default exclusion of that filename, so the reason travels with the rule.
example/pubspec_overrides.yaml
